      "writtenOn": "2026-02-06T19:34:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this is causing us to record a lot of redundant draws+steps when doing chained drawing. For every renderstep inside `recordDraw`, we call `recordBackwards`. While the first render step skips this code, the subsequent steps hit this code and add a new `ChainedDraw`. For something with 2-3 rendersteps, we record 2-3 ChainedDraws per draw and then when we iterate over them when snapping a DrawPass we process the rendersteps multiple times.\n\nWe likely aren\u0027t seeing any visible GM differences because these extra recorded draws will have the same Z value and then fail their depth test, but we\u0027ll still have a lot of CPU overhead writing out the extra instances and performing the vertex shader work before it gets to the fragment work.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 39,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 45,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "d5112d1b7732921920bd084e702feab9e92880f6",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
